{"duration_api_ms":154069,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d0d9eb58-9d0e-4cf0-8abd-21c135414f01","total_cost_usd":0.2152,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15809,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15196,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10357},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15809,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15196,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15809},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15196,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15809,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2152,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10357,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is one curve: D≈3.385 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg, with only flight-path angle varying. Flux rises from about 227k to 274k W/m2 as gamma steepens from -1.5 to -3.565 deg, and bondline temperature falls from 418 to 391 K. Three limits pin the corner. The mass-fraction margin reaches zero at D≈3.3852. The g limit is reached at gamma≈-3.57 deg. The aero surrogate refuses to extrapolate for bluntness ≥1.22 at cone 70 and for (1.2, 69). Hypervolume has saturated at 0.355, so this round fills the gaps along the gamma curve and probes the corner limits.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-a29bfeb09454, C-c197169fbbea, C-5b7da58ad0af, C-064ad9f5e91d, C-c89ccbca6e15 and C-3f1d8b1bcb6a show a smooth flux-versus-temperature trade along gamma at D=3.385, with gaps of 0.2-0.3 deg between -2.05 and -3.1.\",\"C-f71f4a44911d (gamma -3.565, g 11.991) and C-6146d28a8413, C-2a109f1c4205, C-053e6577c074 (gamma -3.58, g 12.002-12.014, infeasible) place the g limit near gamma -3.569 to -3.570.\",\"The mass-fraction margin falls about 0.59 per m of D. At b=1.2 it is 0.01486 at D=3.36 (C-2a109f1c4205), 0.0031 at 3.38 (C-053e6577c074), 1.45e-4 at 3.385 and 8.6e-5 at 3.3851 (C-8b8656d1393f), so the cap is D≈3.38525.\",\"At D=3.36, C-0968b66c7c61 (b=1.0) has margin 0.0095 and C-2a109f1c4205 (b=1.2) has 0.01486. Higher bluntness therefore raises the D cap slightly, by roughly 0.045 m per unit bluntness.\",\"C-11ae4eb65bbb, C-f414065c6995, C-660a8eef4199 and C-35e288c12205 (b 1.22-1.25) and C-460ff98d4dde (b 1.2, cone 69) failed with cd_fore extrapolation errors. C-0a1dd43d842b (1.19, 69.95) and C-b80fd27a21c5 (1.15, 69.3) evaluated normally.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux scales roughly as sqrt(rho_peak/Rn), so larger D and larger bluntness lower it (this is prior knowledge, consistent with the tables). A steeper gamma shortens the heat pulse and lowers bondline temperature until max_g binds, since g depends mainly on gamma. The front is therefore the one-dimensional gamma sweep at the largest D that mass fraction allows. Interpolating in the gaps adds a little hypervolume. Slightly raising bluntness or D at the corner would cut flux by 0.1-0.5%, but only if the surrogate hull allows it.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The 1.205 and 1.21 bluntness probes may hit the surrogate hull boundary and return no geometry; the hull edge between 1.2 and 1.22 is unknown. Predicted margins near the mass and g limits are within about 1e-4 of zero, so the corner points may land infeasible. Gap-fill predictions are linear interpolations between neighbouring evaluated points, and I have no data on regions far from this corner.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.385 at gamma -1.5 slightly beats the D=3.383 front point C-fb90f652dec5 on flux, extending the low-flux end of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227210,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cheap improvement at the extreme end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.5 and -1.6 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.06,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.6 and -1.7 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":230200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.7 and -1.8 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.85,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.8 and -1.9 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.85},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":234400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.9 and -2.05 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.97},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.05 and -2.35 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"This is one of the larger remaining gaps on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.35 and -2.65 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"This is one of the larger remaining gaps on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.65 and -2.9 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.78},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":255600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.9 and -3.1 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -3.1 and -3.28 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -3.28 and -3.4 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -3.4 and -3.55 deg on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.46},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap just below the corner, between -3.5 and -3.55 deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.42,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front densification near the knee of the trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Extrapolating the g slope of about 1.7 per deg puts the limit at gamma≈-3.5695, so -3.567 at D=3.385 should stay feasible while stepping past the previous best point at -3.565.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.567},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274460,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.13,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the g limit at the corner; a small gain in temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"The mass-fraction cap is D≈3.38525, so D=3.3852 keeps a margin of about 2.7e-5. Combined with gamma -3.569 near the g limit, this should give the lowest flux and temperature at the corner.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.569},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274510,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.11,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the joint mass-fraction and g corner; a small hypervolume increment is possible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.205 lowers flux by roughly 0.2% and raises the mass-fraction margin by about 1.3e-4, allowing D=3.3853. It may lie outside the surrogate hull.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.205,\"diameter_m\":3.3853,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.15,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes whether the hull allows bluntness slightly above 1.2; a success would move the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.21 with D=3.3855 (mass margin about 1e-4) probes further toward the hull edge for a flux gain of about 0.4%.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.21,\"diameter_m\":3.3855,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests where the aero surrogate hull ends between bluntness 1.2 (evaluated) and 1.22 (refused).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.205 at a mid-front gamma of -3.4. If the higher bluntness is accepted, it should improve the mid-front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.205,\"diameter_m\":3.3853,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A second, independent probe of bluntness above 1.2 at a different gamma, so a single failure does not settle the question.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":118083,"type":"result","duration_ms":154129,"uuid":"77f91c2b-b633-4b4a-ade9-9720e8030b71","ttft_stream_ms":1613,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1613,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
